course: dictionary
lesson: 6771
title: Seizing the opportunity
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An opportunity is a time when you can do something you want or need to do. It is another word for a chance. «The school has an opportunity for every child to join a club.» The sentence tells you the club is open to you, and you can take it if you want.
explain: Look at the words around opportunity. «Alice was very glad to get an opportunity of showing off a little of her knowledge.» Glad tells you Alice liked the chance, and showing off her knowledge tells you what she planned to do with it. So an opportunity is a chance to do something you are good at or want to do.
explain: Some phrases use opportunity in set ways. To take the opportunity means to use the chance. To miss an opportunity means to let it go by. «A golden opportunity» means a really great chance. When you meet a phrase, read the whole sentence to work out what it means.
fact: An opportunity is a time or situation when it is possible to do something you want or need to do; a chance.
fact: An opportunity can also be a chance for a job or for a better life.
fact: «Take the opportunity» means use the chance when it comes.
fact: «Miss an opportunity» means let a chance go by without using it.
fact: The Mars rover named «Opportunity» worked on Mars for years until a dust storm in 2018 covered its solar panels, and it never woke again.
exercise: «The school has an opportunity for every child to join a club.» What does opportunity mean here? | A test you must pass | *A chance to do something | A rule about school dinners | A kind of club
exercise: What does «a golden opportunity» mean? | A long wait | A bad mistake | *A really great chance | A gold coin
exercise: Find and copy one word from «Alice was very glad to get an opportunity of showing off a little of her knowledge» that shows she liked the chance. | little | *glad | showing | knowledge
test: «Lee decided to take the opportunity and joined the swimming team.» What did Lee do? | Forgot about school | Gave the chance to a friend | *Used the chance to do something he wanted | Let the chance go by
test: What does «miss an opportunity» mean? | *Let a chance go by without using it | Win a prize | Find a lost bag | Use a chance to go to the park
exam: Which phrase means a really great chance? | *a golden opportunity | a missed opportunity | a tired opportunity | a sleepy opportunity
